                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As you can see from the trailer, this goes further than most retro games into creating an \"authentic\" NES look and feel.\n\nThat includes \"NES difficulty,\" and I don't just mean the game is hard. It's hard in the dumb, janky ways that a lot of NES games were. I mean really annoying enemies with placements that are complete BS to deal with. Hope you like climbing a ladder with an enemy camping at the top of it (of course you will get hit by touching him).\n\nBut this is a fun challenge if you're up for that. You can loop it like an arcade game, with neat things happening when you beat it more than once in a row.\n\nCombat is very similar to Zelda II with sub-weapons from Castlevania thrown in. You can find randomized upgrades as you go, which will dramatically affect how your run goes.\n\nIf you're man enough, play this sht.\n\nOh, and the CRT mode is very nice.\n\n--- Update 7/14/2017: Once you've beaten the game multiple times and gotten the good ending, it becomes a bit too RNG-dependent. My runs consistently succeed or fail based on whether I find a specific item during the run. I still recommend the game since I had a really good time with it up until this point.",
